\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 ANTIHUNTER DIGI NODE\
\fs28 TIER 1 \'96 FULLY ASSEMBLED UNIT
\f0\b0\fs22 \cf1 \
\
Built, soldered and bench-tested. Meshtastic is flashed on the radio with the serial link to the node already configured.\
\
\
\f1\b IN THE BOX
\f0\b0 \
\
Assembled node, 8 GB microSD fitted\
Active GPS helix antenna\
2.4 GHz WiFi/BLE SMA antenna\
LoRa SMA antenna for your region\
\
You supply: two 18650 cells.\
\
\
\f1\b SET IT UP
\f0\b0 \
\
1. Screw on the antennas. Finger tight, then an eighth of a turn. Never power the node with the LoRa antenna missing.\
\
2. Fit two 18650 cells, correct orientation, same brand and capacity.\
\
3. Flash AntiHunter on the ESP32 over USB. Web flasher: lukeswitz.github.io/AntiHunter. Pick Full for the web UI, or Headless for quiet field ops.\
\
4. Set the LoRa region on the radio. It ships UNSET, which means receive only, and the node will not answer over mesh until you set it.\
\
5. Change the Bluetooth pairing pin on the radio. Every unit ships with the same one.\
\
6. Make your own encrypted Meshtastic channel primary and turn the public default channel off.\
\
7. Full firmware: join the \f1\b Antihunter\f0\b0  WiFi AP, password \f1\b antihunt3r123\f0\b0 , open http://192.168.4.1 and change those credentials first.\
\
\
\f1\b POWER
\f0\b0 \
\
Regulated 5 V only, from USB or the UPS board. Never wire cells or an unregulated supply to the PCB. One USB cable at a time: the ESP32 and the radio share the power rails.\
\
